"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫I despised life at the brothel.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫The men who came to buy their services "
"were disgusting buffoons—the kind of people who would think they could deceive God. ⟪k:5⟫And the "
"women fawning over them were just as repulsive.⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫That said, I had nowhere else to "
"go, ⟪k:9⟫which meant I was forced to suffer that sickening place."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　창관 생활은 처음에는 끔찍하기만 했어요.⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫　손님으로 오는 남자들도 추잡하여, 주님을 "
"등진 어리석은 자들 뿐.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫　이를 상대로 아양을 떠는 여자들도 똑같이 추잡했어요.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫　"
"하지만 거기서 나온들 제가 갈 데는 있지도 않았어요.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫　그래서 끔찍한 나날을 인내할 수밖에 "
"없었죠."

#: search2:search2_4DED1AF3_6BFA_4E24_AF85_57D0F1A62035
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: e0dc372b12722021e0a3b7c43e47b40e7bd38e7c6b2c6d85dd27c9fa9cf64403
#. default-sha256: 68c0e85e8175a2d59e8aa4ca3fb6a6fc601a379b6a6801c2c19fbbb0813b83d9
msgctxt "search2:search2_4DED1AF3_6BFA_4E24_AF85_57D0F1A62035"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫But by the time a year or so had passed... ⟪k:2⟫my feelings about it had changed.⟪k:3⟫"
"⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫The women of the brothel took good care of me, treating me like a sister. ⟪k:6⟫At "
"first, it was just irritating—I was a ⟪k:7⟫saint⟪k:8⟫, and how could a saint have prostitutes for "
"sisters? ⟪k:9⟫But over time, I got to know them better—grew to appreciate their circumstances and "
"hardships.⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫Despite barely having enough money to keep food on the table, "
"whenever they had a little to spare, they would use it to purchase medicine. ⟪k:14⟫Ointments to "
"apply to my arms, legs, and face. ⟪k:15⟫And as a result of their generosity, my arms and legs "
"started looking almost human—but nothing had any effect on my face."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　그런데 1년 정도 지나고 보니…….⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫　제 인식도 점점 바뀌기 시작했어요.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫　창녀"
"들은 저를 막내 동생처럼 대하며 보살펴 주었어요.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫　처음에는 그것도 짜증스러웠어요. ⟪k:7⟫저"
"는 성녀니까 창녀의 동생이어선 안 되거든요. ⟪k:8⟫하지만, 그렇죠…… 같이 살다 보니, 창녀들의 처지와 "
"고난에 찌든 생활 등이 차츰 이해가 되더라고요.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫　창녀들은 일용할 양식도 궁하면서 돈"
"이 조금 생기면 약을 샀어요. ⟪k:12⟫……제 사지와 얼굴에 바를 약을요. ⟪k:13⟫그 덕분에 사지 쪽은 많이 "
"나아졌지만, 얼굴은 나을 기미가 없었어요."

#: search2:search2_49868C07_5C7F_4310_8998_67F1CCED4A33
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: d3233296dc95d121ae6f768ee7b91e67417f50a5fdb023ca4ee4ffefaa5a3c70
#. default-sha256: 19e5e42797de03deb448e616029595ec5101b863804b383666adaef16124ca09
msgctxt "search2:search2_49868C07_5C7F_4310_8998_67F1CCED4A33"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫My time at the brothel was probably, all things considered, one of the brighter "
"chapters of my life. ⟪k:2⟫There, I was neither saint nor witch, but an ordinary human girl. ⟪k:3⟫"
"For the first time, I felt like my life had meaning beyond my assumed “divine purpose”; I was "
"even beginning to feel kind of happy.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫And with each passing day, my intractable "
"worldview was gaining a little flexibility."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　창관 생활은 제 인생에선 행복한 축에 들었어요.⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫　거기서 저는 성녀나 마녀가 아닌 한 "
"인간이었어요.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫　저는 비로소 인간으로서 사는 의미를 느꼈고, 기쁨을 얻기 시작했어요. ⟪k:5⟫"
"이와 동시에 제 고정관념도 점차 사라져 갔죠."

#: search2:search2_7C67598C_FBF3_41D9_9824_3D3554D47F21
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 79cc43fc0f7f6dd221083b3a25529cc5376fdc81abf50a7672a81d050d002e5f
#. default-sha256: c03bd0339f96ef3e5d6557fd1e64694bf96cfe50e8e96511e671ddd3f900dff9
msgctxt "search2:search2_7C67598C_FBF3_41D9_9824_3D3554D47F21"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫But for some reason...⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫For some reason, happiness always seems to slip "
"away as soon as you’ve got your hands around it. ⟪k:5⟫No one sincerely ⟪k:6⟫wants⟪k:7⟫ to lose "
"it, so why must they?⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫I certainly didn’t mind not being miserable."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　하지만 어째서.⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫　행복이란 느낀 순간에 사라지는 걸까요? ⟪k:3⟫누구도 원해서 잃는 게 "
"아닌데. ⟪k:4⟫네, 저도 행복한 시간이…… 결코 싫지 않았어요."

#: search2:search2_0E96566D_520E_4A59_8C90_C49A7098D6B5
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 265ed80929376a80495c25bea8f615b4748628e1bd476721d151061bad9f1fdd
#. default-sha256: 6bb83835dda0f5ac57a873970483a7f11bb846ac5df38d594c47dd0a7bd9db7e
msgctxt "search2:search2_0E96566D_520E_4A59_8C90_C49A7098D6B5"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The carriage was packed so tight you could barely see the floor—and it smelled like "
"death. ⟪k:2⟫Sweat, urine, feces—every foul odor imaginable compressed into a tiny space.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫"
"⟪k:5⟫There were both men and women there, nearly all of them muttering or groaning or weeping."
"⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫Everyone was young, ripe to be put to work."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　마차 안은 사람들이 꽉꽉 들어차 악취가 났어요. ⟪k:1⟫사람의 땀, 분뇨, 그런 게 뒤섞인 짐승 같"
"은 냄새. ⟪k:2⟫다들 비탄에 빠져 탄식만 흘렸어요.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫　여자도 있거니와 남자도 있었어요. ⟪k:5⟫"
"그 대다수가 노동력이 될 법한 젊은이들이었죠."

#: search2:search2_BEA891AE_D9B6_4C23_B721_07C3F608C144
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 353f2755c28224e484167b799346deaf9cefc9f9d999d4b4ea261c468d214dda
#. default-sha256: 04373ff999fcb1c754b5d1ef5227ad4c56253c6381edb5ea23bab9219d93ad59
msgctxt "search2:search2_BEA891AE_D9B6_4C23_B721_07C3F608C144"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫It didn’t take me long to realize what fate awaited these people—and me.⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫And "
"when I did, I just sat there in silence.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫Then, for the first time, I cried.⟪k:7⟫"
"⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫I was experiencing, I believe, a very human emotion. ⟪k:10⟫I was sad. ⟪k:11⟫Hurt that I "
"had been taken away from a place where I was happy. ⟪k:12⟫From the women at the brothel—and that "
"young man. ⟪k:13⟫It crushed me.⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫And no longer did I wonder why such a "
"thing was happening to “the holy daughter of God.”⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫⟪k:20⟫⟪k:21⟫Something about my "
"tears must have seemed strange to him, because one man saw me and said,"
msgstr ""
"　노예 운송 마차란 걸 바로 이해했어요.⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫　저는 거기서 가만히 있었어요.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫　가만히 "
"있으면서―― 처음으로 눈물을 흘렸죠.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫　그건 매우 인간적인 감정이었을 거예요.⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫　슬"
"펐어요. ⟪k:8⟫행복한 순간이 무너진 게. ⟪k:9⟫창녀들과 그 청년하고 이별한 게. ⟪k:10⟫그게 진심으로…… "
"괴로웠어요.⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫　그때 가선 「주님의 아이인 내가 왜」란 생각은 들지도 않았어요.⟪k:14⟫"
"⟪k:15⟫　그런 제 눈물이 기묘했던 걸까요. ⟪k:16⟫한 남자가 제게 말을 걸었어요."

#: search2:search2_67093575_F906_4D09_AA64_8794D0C8082F
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 46a1cfacc75a1367076516496d506d35fa185f262a157315ab71d18c7c79e76d
#. default-sha256: 293780e1033a1b0b5b9d2b3a2bc3f9691c3246191e144ddf44a6a2f900d43215
msgctxt "search2:search2_67093575_F906_4D09_AA64_8794D0C8082F"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫He was a curious man. ⟪k:2⟫To start, he looked very different from anyone else. ⟪k:3⟫"
"The color of his skin. The length of his nose. The shape of his eyes. ⟪k:4⟫Everything about him "
"was new and unusual.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫Hesitantly, I replied,"
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　매우 특이한 남자였어요. ⟪k:1⟫외모부터가 우리하곤 많이 달랐거든요. ⟪k:2⟫피부색, 코 높이, 눈"
"매. ⟪k:3⟫제가 난생 처음 보는 외모였어요.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫　저는 당혹하면서도 대답했어요."

#: search2:search2_F016AF4F_74FC_4380_A01F_A7586C0A1EBC
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: b2b7a47a57a0304d445db00ec088381bd6fe559e2bb936d1170b1ffa9ed5dbd8
#. default-sha256: 624215b3c65226edf2b77fe279fc33891ed07082704da45ce102a662a12ddfb3
msgctxt "search2:search2_F016AF4F_74FC_4380_A01F_A7586C0A1EBC"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The man fell silent, looking as though he was deep in thought. ⟪k:2⟫I had no idea why "
"he had asked me that, but something about him made me uncomfortable, so I couldn’t bring myself "
"to ask.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫Several hours later, the man suddenly stood up. ⟪k:7⟫The guards had no "
"patience for anyone stepping out of line, and they didn’t look like they would hesitate to kill "
"us either. ⟪k:8⟫So, unsurprisingly, one at the back of the carriage drew his sword and pointed it "
"at the man.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫What ⟪k:12⟫was⟪k:13⟫ surprising, though, was what happened next. "
"⟪k:14⟫The man—his hands shackled like the rest of us—leapt for the guard, slamming his fists into "
"his face and stealing his sword."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　그러자 남자는 침묵하더니, 무슨 생각에 잠겼어요. ⟪k:1⟫저는 도대체 왜 그런 질문을 한 건지 알 "
"수 없었죠. ⟪k:2⟫하지만 조금 무서운 분위기를 풍기는 남자였기에, 제가 질문하긴 꺼려졌어요.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫"
"⟪k:5⟫　마차가 몇 시간 더 달린 때였을까요. ⟪k:6⟫그 남자가 불쑥 일어섰어요. ⟪k:7⟫함부로 행동하면 욕"
"설을 듣는 데다, 심하면 목숨도 빼앗겨요. ⟪k:8⟫그러니 후속 보초가 검을 뽑아 그 남자에게 겨눈 건 당연"
"한 결과였죠.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫　당연한 게 사라진 건 그 다음부터였어요.⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫　남자는 보초에게 달려"
"들어 얼굴을 가격한 후, 날랜 솜씨로 검을 빼앗았어요. ⟪k:13⟫저희 양손에는 수갑이 채워져서 자유롭게 "
"움직일 수 없는 상태였어요. ⟪k:14⟫그 남자는 그런 제약 속에서 그런 행동을 해낸 거예요."

#: search2:search2_3C6B1FA8_F8E3_439D_AAA6_9EE22F657EA5
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: ca4866e697fb27f0d9d873a556a59396890e00ee8a9300427e9274735706bebf
#. default-sha256: 319a4cac152a167cd6b5908c7caefdeb2e18fbc5d8881fab2456500438fed0b3
msgctxt "search2:search2_3C6B1FA8_F8E3_439D_AAA6_9EE22F657EA5"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The entire carriage was in shock. ⟪k:2⟫The guards were too stunned to effectively "
"react, so they were quickly cut down. ⟪k:3⟫And because the one-man uprising had taken place "
"between cities, there was no one the slave traders could ask for help before they were "
"slaughtered.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫In the blink of an eye, it was all over.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫And there was "
"nothing “human” about what I had witnessed. ⟪k:10⟫If I had to describe it, I would say it was as "
"though a wild beast had attacked.⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫The man ruffled through the slave "
"traders’ clothes until he found the keys, which he brought to me, ordering I unshackle him. ⟪k:15⟫"
"And so I did as he commanded.⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫Once they had had enough time to process what had "
"happened, the would-be slaves applauded. ⟪k:19⟫Their wretched souls had been saved.⟪k:20⟫⟪k:21⟫"
"⟪k:22⟫⟪k:23⟫And for a moment, I believed so too."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　누구나 경악했어요. ⟪k:1⟫갑작스러운 반역에 다른 보초들도 대응이 늦어서―― 잇따라 목숨을 빼앗"
"겼어요. ⟪k:2⟫가도 한복판에서 일어난 반역이었기에, 노예상인은 구조 요청도 못 하고 그 남자 손에 죽었"
"어요.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫　순식간―― 그 표현밖에 못 하겠네요. ⟪k:5⟫사람이 부리는 재주 같지 않았어요. ⟪k:6⟫이"
"를 테면 짐승 같았죠.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫　남자는 노예상인의 시체에서 열쇠를 챙기더니, 제게 다가와 수갑"
"을 풀라 했어요. ⟪k:10⟫저는 시키는 대로 했어요.⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫　노예상인에게 끌려가던 딱한 사람들은 그"
"걸 보고 갈채했어요. ⟪k:13⟫그 남자가 노예상인에게서 저희를 구한 줄 알았거든요.⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫　"
"네――, 저도 그 순간에는 같은 생각을 했어요."

#: search2:search2_CE646FAE_59F9_4D8C_A4C3_260A04AA21CF
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 7d0fb29dd272c1d62377c9e7e3a17b6b003d42557d76c30600ea8534626b63a9
#. default-sha256: 2ba22091a653b864bf3f6bc9774e3f27c2e8a7a2cdcfbcd801a6e975743c0089
msgctxt "search2:search2_CE646FAE_59F9_4D8C_A4C3_260A04AA21CF"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫When the man’s hands were free, he rolled his shoulders a couple times, made sure "
"everything was in place, ⟪k:2⟫and then, ⟪k:3⟫he began his massacre.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫Screams of "
"agony filled the carriage as he ran his sword through the helpless men and women packed inside "
"it. ⟪k:7⟫Blood and guts were splattered against every surface. ⟪k:8⟫And those who tried to escape "
"did not get far before being mercilessly skewered.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫It was like a scene out of a "
"nightmare.⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫I was frozen in place. ⟪k:16⟫Not out of fear, but because my "
"mind had shut down. ⟪k:17⟫I couldn’t make sense of what was happening, so my mind rejected it. "
"⟪k:18⟫And with my brain having given up, my body was no more than a lifeless puppet."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫　남자는 완전히 자유로워지자, 팔을 빙빙 돌리며 자기 몸 상태를 확인했어요.⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫　그리고"
"――⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫　노예들을 차례차례 죽였죠.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫　몸도 움직이기 힘든 마차 안에서 아비규환이 터졌"
"어요. ⟪k:7⟫마차 안이 피와 내장으로 가득 찼어요. ⟪k:8⟫남자는 도망치려고 마차에서 뛰어내린 사람도 가"
"차없이 찔러 죽였어요.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫　몹시―― 비현실적인 광경이었어요.⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫　저는 꼼짝도 "
"못 했어요. ⟪k:14⟫무서워서 그런 게 아니라, 아무 생각도 못 했거든요. ⟪k:15⟫눈앞에서 일어나는 사태가 "
"납득이 안 돼서 받아들이지 못 했어요. ⟪k:16⟫사고를 잃은 저는 손끝 하나 못 움직였어요."

#: search2:search2_ED75D9A8_09AE_49FE_AB90_631A4242816B
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 82b11d512677803a97ca983787d1a5ce880346a4a38ce656c4d84de93b12e7c7
#. default-sha256: 7bfa535b0247c84ed6ae4c3591e4f93e3c9f653819ed5182afb7af66e71e6d54
msgctxt "search2:search2_ED75D9A8_09AE_49FE_AB90_631A4242816B"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫In short order, all the slaves were dead, and I was sitting in a "
"pool of blood staring at the man. ⟪k:6⟫He pointed his blade at me, and with a little smirk, said, "
"“Why didn’t you run?”⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫In turn, I asked him, “Why did you kill them?”⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫"
"⟪k:12⟫The smile vanished from his face, and after a few quiet moments of pondering, he replied, "
"“Because I felt like it.”⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫“And why haven’t you killed me yet?” I asked.⟪k:16⟫"
"⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫To which he gave a curt, “I don’t know,” then withdrew his blade and wandered off "
"into the distance."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫　머지않아 노예들이 몰살당해 모든 게 피투성이가 되었어요. ⟪k:5⟫남은 건 저"
"와 그 남자 뿐이었죠.⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫　남자는 제게도 검을 겨누었어요. ⟪k:8⟫그리고 실실 웃으며 「왜 안 도"
"망치지」라 물었어요.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫　저는 「왜 사람들을 죽이셨나요」라 되물었어요.⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫　남자"
"는 정색하여 잠깐 침묵한 후, 나직이 「그러고 싶어서」라 대답했어요.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫　저는 이어서 「왜 "
"저를 바로 안 죽이시죠」라 물었어요.⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫　그 말에 남자는 「모르겠다」고 하더니, 검을 거두"
"곤 어디론가 떠났어요."

